From bd3e1e90ce054175f8f8594c15338cde0bbc75d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lavender3533 <104026084+Lavender3533@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:45:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: faster PTQ1_0 mat-vec on RDNA1

Rewrite the dedicated PTQ1_0 mat-vec kernel so a 32-lane team works on one
block at a time with one packed byte per lane. Activation loads become
coalesced and are reused across all rows of the workgroup; trits are decoded
once per row pair (two rows packed into 16-bit halves) and reused across all
columns of a small-batch mat-vec.

Rows per workgroup default to 16 on RDNA1 (measured best on an RX 5700 XT),
other architectures keep the previous default. GGML_VK_PTQ1_ROWS and
GGML_VK_PTQ1_MIN_ROWS override.

RX 5700 XT, test-backend-ops perf, PTQ1_0 x f32:
  m=17408 k=5120 n=1: 266 us -> 168 us
  m=17408 k=5120 n=8: 2117 us -> 901 us
test-backend-ops MUL_MAT ptq1_0: 168/168 passed.
